+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:15:51 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 13/46] windowing: name the stereoscopic layout wherever a mode
+ is logged
+
+A mode's strMode is its geometry, scan type and refresh rate, which does not
+distinguish a half 3D mode from the 2D mode of the same timing: both print as
+"1920x1080 @ 50.000000 Hz". So no log line said which layout was being signalled,
+or whether 3D was signalled at all. Frame packing was identifiable only by
+accident, its packed scanout giving it a geometry of its own.
+
+The cost of that is not hypothetical. "Display resolution ADJUST : 1920x1080 @
+23.976080 Hz (48)" is LOGINFO, the line to hand when someone has not enabled
+debug logging, and it cannot answer the first question asked of it. Which mode a
+resolution index names could only be recovered by counting through the mode
+enumeration and adding RES_CUSTOM. And the enumeration itself printed the 3D
+variants identically to their 2D twins, so CLog collapsed them as duplicate
+messages - the layouts a display offers had to be guessed from which timings the
+HDMI specification makes each layout mandatory for, which is a guess that can be
+wrong.
+
+So add the layout to RESOLUTION_INFO, as a tag to append: the separator belongs to
+the tag and a 2D mode's tag is empty, so those lines read exactly as they did.
+Name it at the four places a mode is described - the resolution enumeration, the
+ADJUST line, the native 3D mode match and the arrangement change - and tell frame
+packing from the half top-and-bottom layout it is presented as by iBlanking, which
+only a packed scanout has.
+
