+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:27:07 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 16/46] DVDDemuxFFmpeg: read the stereoscopic mode from
+ AVStereo3D side data
+
+Kodi learned a stream's stereoscopic layout from exactly two places: the
+Matroska stereo_mode tag, and the asf/wmv Stereoscopic/StereoscopicLayout pair.
+An mp4 or mov that declares its layout in the container - through the
+QuickTime vexu/eyes boxes, an mkv-to-mp4 remux carrying a stereo3d box, or an
+SEI frame packing arrangement the decoder promotes - was played flat, because
+none of that reaches the AVDictionary the two existing paths read.
+
+ffmpeg already parses all of it and normalises the result into an AVStereo3D
+exported as AV_PKT_DATA_STEREO3D on codecpar->coded_side_data. Read it in the
+same place, and with the same av_packet_side_data_get() idiom, as the Dolby
+Vision, HDR and display matrix side data just above, and map AVStereo3DType
+onto the matroska vocabulary Kodi uses internally.
+
+AV_STEREO3D_FLAG_INVERT means the right or bottom view holds the left eye, so
+it selects between the _lr and _rl spelling of each layout. Types with no Kodi
+equivalent - side by side quincunx, and the unspecified type used for streams
+whose views are coded separately rather than packed - map to nothing and leave
+the stream untagged, which is what happens today.
+
+Side data wins over the metadata tags, which stay as the fallback, so Matroska
+and asf behaviour is unchanged.
+
+(cherry picked from commit 977f2070c4c2ee50035a753573e173ad792bdc4e)
