index 0000000000..deb31d4054
--- /dev/null
+++ b/projects/RPi/devices/RPi5/patches/kodi/0020-DVDInputStreamBluray-let-libbluray-choose-the-player.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:21:17 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 20/46] DVDInputStreamBluray: let libbluray choose the player
+ profile
+
+A Blu-ray 3D disc decides the player cannot do 3D. Its first play object
+takes the branch that parks on a still telling you to connect a 3D player,
+and nothing gets past it.
+
+We announce profile 6 before the disc is opened, leaving the profile version
+register reading 0x0310. libbluray raises the profile itself once it has read
+the index -- profile 6 for a UHD disc, profile 5 for a 3D one -- but the 3D
+half of that will not run over a profile the application has already asked
+for, and gives up on finding a version of 0x0300 or higher. The output
+preference, display capability and profile registers are then left as they
+were, and the disc reads them as a 2D player. The same disc opened by
+CBlurayDirectory, which announces no profile, gets its 3D registers.
+
+Announcing it was never needed. libbluray forces the UHD initialisation, so a
+UHD disc has those registers written whatever we did beforehand; all we
+achieved was to suppress the 3D case. Say nothing and let the disc decide.
+Kept for libbluray older than 1.1.0, which does not raise the profile itself.
+
+(cherry picked from commit 6f52f0e5c9214484ab29d2fd2bab1580d1335928)
+---
+ .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp          | 11 +++++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
