+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:43:22 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 25/46] BlurayOffsetMetadata: read the plane offsets of a 3D
+ dependent view
+
+The depth a "1 plane + offset" title asks of its subtitle plane travels in the MVC
+dependent view, once per GOP, as an SEI: a user_data_unregistered message carrying UUID
+17ee8c60-f84d-11d9-8cd6-0800200c9a66, an "OFMD" marker, a ten byte header and then one
+byte per frame per offset sequence, sequence major. Byte seven of that header is the
+frame count and byte six holds the sequence count in its low six bits, the two above it
+being markers. An offset byte is a direction bit and a seven bit magnitude rather than a
+signed value, which is why an unused sequence reads 0x80 - a magnitude of nothing, the
+same offset whichever way it points.
+
+The message is found by its UUID rather than by walking the SEI messages, because how it
+is wrapped varies. Encoders nest it in mvc_scalable_nesting under either form of that
+message's header - one disc here writes the one byte form, another the two byte one -
+and there is no reason to think those are the only two. A sixteen byte UUID is its own
+evidence, and nothing outside an SEI NAL of the dependent view is searched.
+
+COffsetMetadataStore holds the GOPs around the current position: the demuxer fills it in
+as the dependent view is read and the render thread asks for it a moment later, so it
+carries its own lock. A block is indexed by the presentation time of the first frame it
+describes and the length of a frame, which makes a lookup arithmetic rather than a
+search, and only the last few dozen are kept - the demuxer runs no further ahead than
+its buffer, and a seek empties it anyway.
+
+Tests cover both nesting forms, the direction bit, emulation prevention bytes inside the
+message, and the sizes and sequence counts that cannot be right. The parser has also been
+run over a retail disc's dependent view, where its output matches an independent read of
+the same stream sequence for sequence.
+
+(cherry picked from commit 17cbca380a7d26f12d601b50ef17afb694958065)
+---
+ .../DVDDemuxers/BlurayOffsetMetadata.cpp      | 199 +++++++++++++++++
+ .../DVDDemuxers/BlurayOffsetMetadata.h        |  94 ++++++++
+ .../VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/CMakeLists.txt    |   6 +-
+ .../DVDDemuxers/test/CMakeLists.txt           |   3 +-
+ .../test/TestBlurayOffsetMetadata.cpp         | 207 ++++++++++++++++++
+ 5 files changed, 506 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
+ create mode 100644 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/BlurayOffsetMetadata.cpp
+ create mode 100644 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/BlurayOffsetMetadata.h
+ create mode 100644 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/test/TestBlurayOffsetMetadata.cpp
