+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:13:20 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 28/46] StereoscopicsManager: compare the arrangement asked
+ for, not the one on screen
+
+SetStereoMode() records the arrangement wanted and Flip() makes it current, so the
+two differ for the rest of the frame. ApplyStereoMode() compared its target against
+the current one, which left it blind to a request already queued: asked for the
+arrangement the graphics context is about to leave, it saw nothing to do and
+returned, and the queued request stood.
+
+A title starting from a disc menu does exactly that. The outgoing title's
+arrangement is cleared and the incoming one detected within a frame of each other,
+on separate threads, and whichever arrived first won. Where the clearing went first
+the detection was dropped, the flip put the GUI in off, and the display mode search
+- which reads the arrangement asked for rather than the one on screen - then chose a
+plain 2D mode for a stereoscopic source. The setting said one thing and the output
+another, with nothing left to re-apply it, so the picture stayed side by side for
+the rest of the title. Playing that title on its own was fine, having no outgoing
+arrangement to clear.
+
+The reporter of this saw it on one disc of five, and only from its menu. Two
+arrangements 24ms apart lost it, 54ms apart did not.
+
+Compare against GetNextStereoMode(), which is what the graphics context already
+asks callers deciding an output arrangement to use.
+
+(cherry picked from commit 094ae3754ad73cd68c852b1ffe47b67e77a1c0cd)
