+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:06:59 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 29/46] VideoPlayer: let the viewer swap the eyes of a stream
+ that declares its own layout
+
+"Invert stereoscopic 3D mode (flip eyes)" was only read when the picture arrived without a
+layout, which is to say only when the setting beside it was being used to tell Kodi how to
+read a file that says nothing. Anything that declares its own layout took the other branch
+and the toggle did nothing at all.
+
+That is precisely the case where a viewer needs it. A Blu-ray 3D playlist names which coded
+view is the left eye and a Matroska file carries a StereoMode, and either can be wrong -
+there is nothing to check them against, and a disc that says its base view is the left eye
+when it is the right one leaves every scene inside out with no way back. Half-SBS and
+half-TAB files mislabelled by whoever packed them are the same problem.
+
+So invert whatever layout the picture ends up with, from wherever it came. The two settings
+now compose the way they read: one says how the frame is packed, the other says the eyes are
+the other way round.
+
+Verified on a retail Blu-ray 3D disc, where the title plays as left_right, reports
+right_left with the toggle on, and left_right again with it off.
+
+[Bryan Hoban: without STATS_LOG_INTERVAL, from a commit not taken]
