+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:38:09 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 37/46] RendererDRMPRIMEGLES: sample the buffer for the eye
+ being drawn
+
+The GUI is drawn once per eye, and this renderer crops the packed frame to the
+half the current view wants. Where the views arrive as a buffer each there is
+nothing to crop: the eye picks the buffer and the source rectangle stays the whole
+frame, which the shared geometry already leaves alone for a source that is not
+packed.
+
+This is the path a Wayland session takes, where there is no video plane to scan
+out on, and the one a GBM session falls back to when RendererDRMPRIME cannot claim
+a second plane.
+
+The texture cache holds an imported texture per dma-buf and a multiview stream has
+a frame per view in flight, so raise its cap for the same reason as the
+framebuffer cache.
+
+(cherry picked from commit b7deca5d86af547b6996212fc6d1be274d4748ed)
