+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:28:22 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 42/46] VideoPlayer: resume a disc where it was left
+
+Play part of a disc image, stop, and play it again: it starts from the
+beginning. The position was kept, and playing the playlist itself resumes
+correctly, but nothing found it from the disc.
+
+A disc is watched a playlist at a time, so the resume point is stored against
+the playlist that was playing -- bluray://<disc>/BDMV/PLAYLIST/00800.mpls -- and
+that is not what the viewer picks. Looking the image up finds nothing, and a
+disc that has never been played is started from its beginning.
+
+Look for it where it is. A disc offers the resume point of the most recently
+played of its playlists, so it shows as part watched and is offered as a resume,
+and resuming plays that playlist rather than the disc. The playlist has to be
+played rather than the disc because a resume is not a start, so none of the
+searches that pick a playlist run.
+
+(cherry picked from commit 4a4e9b4e8b880ec9750a0cea0c951dbe8189a058)
+---
