+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:06:48 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 44/46] [VideoPlayer] Start an open GOP's plane offsets at its
+ first shown frame
+
+A GOP's offset metadata covers its frames in presentation order,
+starting with the first frame shown. The store anchored it at the
+access unit that carries it, the GOP's keyframe. In an open GOP the
+leading B-frames are decoded after the keyframe but shown before it, so
+every depth change landed one frame late, and each leading frame read
+the previous GOP's last offset.
+
+Lower the anchor to the earliest presentation time among the access
+units that follow the carrier, at most 8 frames back so that a loop or
+a timestamp jump cannot stretch a block. The Blu-ray and the remux path
+both feed it.
+
+Measured on the Alita 3D remux, pairing each table with the access unit
+that carries it: the table's frame count matched the span between first
+shown frames in 82 of 83 GOPs, and the span between carriers in 52.
+Across 225 MVC remuxes in one library, 62 use open GOPs, at two thirds
+of their keyframes; an I/P-only encode such as Hugo is unaffected.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+(cherry picked from commit bc4a0ec4bcf8ecd3fbce30ddea14bdc42a643555)
